Hello Team,
We are pleased to announce that we are now providing GitHub Enterprise Support for PSM customers. Please review the routing guidelines below to ensure cases are assigned correctly.

 ✅ Route to IMS: GitHub Support assignment group when:

The customer has Premier Support for Microsoft offering with a GitHub-related issue.
The customer account contains both a GitHub Special Handling Note and a Company Record Note.
The issue involves a GitHub Enterprise production outage or a business-critical service impact.
 🔍 Common GitHub Enterprise Keywords
Be aware of the following GitHub Enterprise products and technologies when reviewing cases:

GitHub Enterprise Cloud (GHEC)
GitHub Enterprise Server (GHES)
GitHub Actions
GitHub Copilot
GitHub Codespaces
Dependabot
GitHub Advanced Security (GHAS)
Pull Requests (PRs)
GitHub Repositories
GitHub Webhooks
SAML / SSO integration with GitHub
SCIM in gitHub (System for Cross-domain Identity Management)
Enterprise Managed Users (EMU)
GitHub API
Actions Runners
Repository Access
Repository Migrations
⚠️ Important Routing Notes
All onboarded GitHub Enterprise customers will have both a GitHub Special Handling Note and a Company Record Note on their account.
If these notes are not present, only GitHub production outages or business-critical service impact cases should be routed to IMS: GitHub Support.
Do not transfer tickets based solely on GitHub-related keywords. Always validate company's service offering, special handling note, and and company record notes before routing.
CSP customers are not entitled to this service and should be directed to engage their Account Executive (AE) for information on available support options